---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Window from '../components/Window.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const repository = 'https://github.com/gwenlium/gwenlium.github.io';
---

<SiteLayout title="Publishing" noindex>
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Site tools</p><h1>Publishing</h1></header>
  <div class="admin-grid">
    <Window title="publishing / editor">
      <h2>Open the editor</h2>
      <p>This public site has no visitor login. Editing happens in Pages CMS with your GitHub account, not through a login on this page.</p>
      <div class="admin-actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.pagescms.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Icon name="external" size={15} /> Open Pages CMS<span class="sr-only"> (opens a new tab)</span></a></div>
      <ol class="workflow">
        <li>Sign in to Pages CMS with GitHub and authorize access to <a href={repository}>gwenlium/gwenlium.github.io</a>. You need write access to this repository.</li>
        <li>Select the repository and its deployed branch. Pages CMS reads the included <code>.pages.yml</code> configuration.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Devlog</strong> for Markdown entries; use <strong>Site, game &amp; about</strong>, <strong>Gallery</strong>, and <strong>Music</strong> for the other pages. Direct media uploads are disabled; paste prepared preview URLs instead.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://pagescms.org/docs/quick-start/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pages CMS setup guide <Icon name="external" size={12} /><span class="sr-only"> (opens a new tab)</span></a>
    </Window>

    <Window title="important / public repository" tone="pink">
      <div class="privacy-warning"><Icon name="settings" size={28} /><h2>Draft does not mean private.</h2></div>
      <p>This repository is <strong>public</strong>. Draft text and committed files are readable on GitHub as soon as you save them, even when they are excluded from the website.</p>
      <p>Keep original artwork, full recordings, and other private masters <strong>outside the repository</strong>, not just in a gitignored folder. Never upload them to GitHub or Pages CMS. Do not store secrets, private notes, or API keys here; removing a file does not erase Git history.</p>
      <p>GitHub authorization controls who can edit. It does not make the content private.</p>
    </Window>

    <Window title="publishing / prepared media" tone="sage">
      <h2>Import a public preview, not the original</h2>
      <ol class="workflow">
        <li>On your computer, open an up-to-date local checkout and install its dependencies with <code>npm ci</code>. Keep the original file in a separate folder outside that checkout.</li>
        <li>From the checkout, run <code>npm run media:import -- "C:/PrivateMedia/original.png" --name artwork</code>, replacing the path and name with your own. For audio or video, optionally add <code>--start 15 --duration 30</code> to select a short excerpt.</li>
        <li>The importer leaves the original untouched and creates a reduced, visibly watermarked image or video preview, or a short audio preview. Audio and video default to 30 seconds and are limited to 60 seconds. Animated images keep their motion.</li>
        <li>Review the generated preview. Commit and push only its file in <code>public/media</code> and the updated <code>src/content/media-previews.json</code> registry to your publishing branch. Never add the original. Do not edit the registry by hand.</li>
        <li>Copy the exact <code>/media/...</code> URL printed by the importer into the editor’s preview field. For an article image, switch to <strong>Source</strong> and write <code>![A meaningful description](/media/your-prepared-preview.webp)</code>, replacing the URL with the generated one. Save the entry to publish it through the workflow below.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Every public preview can still be downloaded or copied.</strong> Watermarks, reduced image sizes, and short excerpts limit what you share; they are not DRM. The intentionally public profile avatar and site branding are separate. YouTube/Vimeo trailer links remain public on those services.</p>
      <p>If a build rejects missing, unregistered, or changed media, import it again and commit the generated preview with its registry update. A rejected deployment cannot undo a file already committed to a public repository.</p>
    </Window>

    <Window title="publishing / workflow" tone="sage">
      <h2>From draft to published</h2>
      <ol class="workflow">
        <li>Create an entry. New posts start with <strong>Draft</strong> switched on. Write your title, a unique permanent URL slug, a UTC publication date, your excerpt, and your article.</li>
        <li>Use only prepared preview URLs; add cover alternative text and descriptions for media. Keep the permanent URL slug unchanged after publishing.</li>
        <li>Switch <strong>Draft</strong> off and save when ready. Only entries dated today or earlier in UTC are included in the website and RSS.</li>
        <li>Saving commits to GitHub. The deployment workflow validates content, optimizes images, and rebuilds the static site. Check that the deployment succeeds before sharing the link.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Future-dated posts become visible after a successful build on or after their publication date, not at the moment the date changes in your browser.</p>
      <div class="admin-actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href={`${repository}/actions`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Actions status <Icon name="external" size={14} /><span class="sr-only"> (opens a new tab)</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/devlog/">View devlog</a></div>
    </Window>

    <Window title="publishing / email & RSS" tone="lavender">
      <h2>Automatic email updates</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/rss.xml" data-astro-reload>RSS feed</a> updates after each successful deployment. Once your follow.it publisher feed is connected, follow.it sends new-post notifications automatically.</p>
      <ol class="workflow">
        <li>Create or sign in to your <a href="https://follow.it/publish" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">follow.it publisher account<span class="sr-only"> (opens a new tab)</span></a>.</li>
        <li>Add <a href="https://gwenlium.dev/rss.xml">https://gwenlium.dev/rss.xml</a> as your feed and enable automatic email delivery.</li>
        <li>Put the feed’s public subscription URL into <strong>Site, game &amp; about → follow.it subscription URL</strong>. Confirmation, delivery preferences, and unsubscribe are handled by follow.it. Leave the URL empty until your feed is ready.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href="/subscribe/">View subscription options</a>
    </Window>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .admin-grid { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: start; }
  h2 { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  p, .workflow { font-family: var(--font-reading); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--muted); }
  strong { color: var(--ink); }
  code { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: .8em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .workflow { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .workflow li { padding-left: .3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .admin-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; }
  .text-link { display: inline-flex; gap: .5rem; align-items: center; font-size: .75rem; text-underline-offset: .25em; }
  .privacy-warning { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .privacy-warning h2 { margin: 0; }
  .privacy-warning :global(svg) { flex-shrink: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) { .admin-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
